1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,200
Your battery was fine all summer.

2
00:00:02,200 --> 00:00:04,000
First cold morning, it's dead.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
Cold doesn't kill a battery —

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
it exposes one that was already weak.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
One clue: cranking power fades as a battery ages,

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
and cold cuts what's left.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
A battery that starts fine at 70 degrees

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
can fail that same test at 20.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
A load test checks real cranking power —

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
not just a voltage reading.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before the first cold snap.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
